#question(title: [A theorem about limits], centered: true, shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  #slide-block()[
    Let $f$ be a function with domain $RR$
    such that
    $
      lim_(x -> 0) f(x) = 3
    $
    Prove that
    $
      lim_(x -> 0) [5 f(2 x)] = 15
    $
    directly from the definition of limit. Do
    not use any of the limit laws.
  ]

  + Write down the formal definition of the
    statement you want to prove.
  + Write down what the structure of the
    formal proof should be, without filling
    the details.
  + Rough work.
  + Write down a complete proof.
]
